<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajaditya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 949</span> · Also known as Rajaditya Chola</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajaditya was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> crown prince, the eldest son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parantaka-i">Parantaka I</a>, who commanded the Chola forces on the northern frontier of the kingdom. He was killed on his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephant</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-takkolam">Battle of Takkolam</a> in 949, where the Rashtrakuta emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna-iii">Krishna III</a> and his Western Ganga ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butuga-ii">Butuga II</a> defeated the Chola army; Ganga records credit Butuga with his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaditya.jpg" alt="Rajaditya" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E. F. H. Wiele · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atakur_inscription_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
